# Ground Control environment template.
#
# Copy to `.env` in the directory the Ground Control MCP server is launched from
# — normally the consuming repository's root. That file is the ONLY source of
# Ground Control's variables, whether the server was started by Claude Code,
# Codex, or anything else (issue #1562). No machine-level or user-level
# configuration file is consulted, and no variable below falls back to whatever
# the launcher passed down: if it is not in this file, the server does not have
# it, and the tool that needs it refuses with an error naming the variable and
# this file.
#
# That is deliberate. The launch directory is what lets separate checkouts draw
# on resources belonging to different projects or organizations, and what makes
# it possible to deploy Ground Control into a single-repo sandbox. A machine-wide
# file would silently hand a global credential to a repository that deliberately
# has none.
#
# Nothing here is required: the server starts, and every tool that needs no
# variable works, with the file absent. Each variable switches on one optional
# behavior. There is no backend, database, or frontend to configure (issue
# #1500), so a real `.env` still carrying `GC_DATABASE_*`, `GC_REDIS_URL`,
# `GC_SERVER_PORT`, `GC_ADMIN_*`, or `GC_EMBEDDING_*` is carrying dead settings
# that nothing reads.
#
# The file is read once at startup, so a new or rotated value needs a server
# restart. Keep `.env` gitignored and `chmod 600` if you put a real token in it;
# the server reads tokens in-process and never returns them through a tool
# result. `mcp/ground-control/lib/server-env.js` inventories every name below,
# and a contract test keeps that inventory, this template, and the code in
# agreement.
#
# The Citation MCP server (`mcp/citation`) has its own variables. They reach that
# separate process through `.mcp.json` expansion from the MCP client's
# environment, NOT through this file, and are documented in
# `mcp/citation/README.md`.
#
# Replace every placeholder below with a real value only in your local `.env`.

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Ground Control MCP server (mcp/ground-control) — see mcp/ground-control/README.md
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Per-invocation timeout for the Codex-backed tools (architecture preflight and
# review), within the bounds in mcp/ground-control/lib/model-subprocess.js.
# GC_CODEX_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000

# Deadline for each fixed Git/GitHub command run under the /implement publish
# lease or the integration lock (default 10 minutes, capped at 1 hour), and for a
# repository gate shell: the pre-commit hook and the integration completion gate
# (default 30 minutes, capped at 3 hours). See mcp/ground-control/lib/bounded-exec.js.
# GC_COMMAND_TIMEOUT_MS=600000
# GC_GATE_TIMEOUT_MS=1800000

# Run the core and security reviewers concurrently. Only the value 2 does.
# GC_CODEX_REVIEW_PARALLEL=1

# Diff-slice budget for one review cycle, in bytes. Default 262144 (256 KiB).
# GC_CODEX_REVIEW_MAX_DIFF_BYTES=262144

# Extra comma-separated GitHub logins gc_codex_verify_finding accepts as finding
# authors, for a service-identity deployment. The built-in set already covers a
# local developer workflow.
# GH_VERIFY_FINDING_AUTHORS=some-service-account[bot]

# Anthropic key used only by the knowledge-ingest child process, so ingestion can
# bill separately from the review engine.
# GC_KNOWLEDGE_INGEST_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=replace-with-an-anthropic-api-key

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SonarCloud
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Lets gc_watch_sonar_analysis read the quality gate, and is the token the
# sonarqube MCP server in .mcp.json receives. CI supplies its own from secrets.
# Without it the tool returns sonar_watch_token_missing, which /implement Step 11
# treats as an operator provisioning fault rather than as Sonar findings.
# SONAR_TOKEN=replace-with-a-sonarcloud-token

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Review engine (`claude`) — the optional review-cap disposition judge
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# Used only when `workflow.review_disposition.judge.enabled` is true; the
# dedicated test-quality reviewer it also served was removed by ADR-099.
# Declare exactly one auth mode. With none declared the judge refuses before
# spawning `claude` rather than falling
# through to whatever default profile the host happens to have. When Vertex,
# Bedrock, or a dedicated config directory is declared, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY is
# stripped from the child so the declared mode wins; the key is kept when it is
# the only auth declared.

# Vertex AI. CLOUD_ML_REGION and one of the project variables come with it.
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_VERTEX=1
# CLOUD_ML_REGION=global
# GOOGLE_CLOUD_PROJECT=replace-with-a-gcp-project-id
# ANTHROPIC_VERTEX_PROJECT_ID=replace-with-a-gcp-project-id
# GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/absolute/path/to/service-account.json

# Amazon Bedrock.
# CLAUDE_CODE_USE_BEDROCK=1
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
# AWS_PROFILE=replace-with-an-aws-profile
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=replace-with-an-aws-access-key-id
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=replace-with-an-aws-secret-access-key
# AWS_SESSION_TOKEN=replace-with-an-aws-session-token

# A dedicated Claude Code profile directory holding its own credentials.
# CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=/absolute/path/to/a/claude/profile/dir

# Direct API auth. Either one alone is a complete auth mode.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=replace-with-an-anthropic-api-key
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=replace-with-an-anthropic-auth-token

# Gateway or proxy in front of the Anthropic API.
# ANTHROPIC_BASE_URL=https://example.invalid

# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Codex engine — architecture preflight and the pre-push code review
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# `codex` authenticates from its own profile directory when no key is declared,
# so neither of these is required. They are the only Ground Control values
# forwarded to that child besides HOME and PATH.

# OPENAI_API_KEY=replace-with-an-openai-api-key
# CODEX_HOME=/absolute/path/to/a/codex/profile/dir
